<title>USA: Plymouth unit acquires Spanish Tape Co.</title>
<headline>Plymouth unit acquires Spanish Tape Co.</headline>
<dateline>CANTON, Mass. 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Plymouth Rubber Company Inc said on Thursday its wholly owned subsidiary Plymouth Rubber Europa S.A. acquired 100 percent of the shares of Cintas Adhesivas Nunez S.A. in Porrino, Spain through a cash purchase.</p>
<p>Additional terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Cintas Adhesivas Nunez produces vinyl and cloth-based insulating tapes primarily for the Spanish national market. Until its acquisition by Plymouth Rubber, Cintas Adhesivas Nunez was a privately owned company with about $5.0 million in annual sales.</p>
<p>Plymouth Rubber manufactures and distributes rubber and vinyl products.</p>
</text>
